ce and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138, USA. Electronic address: CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}},{"fullName":"Harris JA","lastName":"Harris","firstName":"Julie A","initials":"JA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Allen Institute for Brain Science, Seattle, WA 98109, USA. Electronic address: CONTACT_EMAIL."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-7632-6822"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-0007-7935"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9954-5515"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2540-1153"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"8","volume":"18","journalIssueId":2526793,"dateOfPublication":"2017 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2017,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cell Rep","title":"Cell reports","essn":"2211-1247","issn":"2211-1247","nlmid":"101573691","isoabbreviation":"Cell Rep"},"printPublicationDate":"2017-02-01"},"pubYear":"2017","pageInfo":"2058-2072","abstractText":"Understanding how >30 types of retinal ganglion cells (RGCs) in the mouse retina each contribute to visual processing in the brain will require more tools that label and manipulate specific RGCs. We screened and analyzed retinal expression of Cre recombinase using 88 transgenic driver lines. In many lines, Cre was expressed in multiple RGC types and retinal cell classes, but several exhibited more selective expression. We comprehensively mapped central projections from RGCs labeled in 26 Cre lines using viral tracers, high-throughput imaging, and a data processing pipeline. We identified over 50 retinorecipient regions and present a quantitative retina-to-brain connectivity map, enabling comparisons of target-specificity across lines. Projections to two major central targets were notably correlated: RGCs projecting to the outer shell or core regions of the lateral geniculate projected to superficial or deep layers within the superior colliculus, respectively. Retinal images and projection data are available online at http://connectivity.brain-map.org.","affiliation":"Center for Brain Science and Department of Molecular and Cellular Biology, Harvard University, Cambridge, MA 02138, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article","Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"NS029169","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIMH NIH HHS","acronym":"MH","grantId":"U01 MH105960","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"P30EY012196","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NINDS NIH HHS","acronym":"NS","grantId":"R01 NS029169","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NEI NIH HHS","acronym":"EY","grantId":"P30 EY012196","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NINDS NIH HHS","acronym":"NS","grantId":"R37 NS029169","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NEI NIH HHS","acronym":"EY","grantId":"R01 EY022073","orderIn":0},{"agency":"National Institutes of Health","grantId":"EY022073","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Visual Pathways","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Retinal Ganglion Cells","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Retina","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"PH","qualifierName":"physiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Transgenic"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Integrases","meshQua